 "rules": {
  "R1_headroom": "At b in {3, 2}: explanation headroom exists at b bits iff the mean over folds of LCI_val(uniform-channel-4bit) - LCI_val(uniform-channel-b bit) >= 0.05.",
  "R2_beats": "XGQ beats a comparator M at budget B iff all hold over the folds: (a) mean LCI_val gain >= 0.02; (b) LCI_val strictly higher in >= ceil(0.8 * n_folds) folds (an identical allocation counts as not higher); (c) mean F1_val >= M's - 0.01; (d) mean worst-subject LCI_val >= M's - 0.01.",
  "R3_claim": "XGQ beats existing allocation at B iff it beats every comparator at B: zeroq_kl, hawq, and (3bit budget only) the uniform per-channel 3-bit model of the same size. The contribution is supported iff R3 holds at >= 1 budget whose bit width has headroom under R1 (3bit -> 3; 2.5bit -> 3 or 2; 2.25bit -> 2). Otherwise it is reported as not supported; nothing is retuned.",
